# File Headers

All JavaScript files must include a standardized header block following this exact format:

## Required Header Format

```javascript
// =============================================================================
// NOBLE ARCHITECTURE - [MODULE NAME]
// =============================================================================
//
// FILE       : [FileName.js]
// NAMESPACE  : [App.ModuleName]
// MODULE     : [ModuleName]
// AUTHOR     : Adam Noble - Noble Architecture
// PURPOSE    : [Brief purpose statement]
// CREATED    : 31-Jan-2026
//
// DESCRIPTION:
// - [Bullet point description]
// - [Additional details]
//
// -----
//
// DEVELOPMENT LOG:
// 31-Jan-2026 - Version 1.0.0
// - Initial Stable Release
//   - Blah
//
// 19-Jan-2026 - Version 0.1.0
// - Beta Version
//   - Blah
//
// =============================================================================
```

## Header Components

### Top Banner
- Use `=` characters for top-level module banners
- Format: `NOBLE ARCHITECTURE - [MODULE NAME]`
- Always uppercase for "NOBLE ARCHITECTURE"

### Metadata Section
- **FILE:** The actual filename with extension
- **NAMESPACE:** The global namespace path (e.g., `NaProjectAdmin.ConfigManager`)
- **MODULE:** The module name without prefixes
- **AUTHOR:** Always "Adam Noble - Noble Architecture"
- **PURPOSE:** Single line describing the module's purpose
- **CREATED:** Date in DD-MMM-YYYY format (e.g., 31-Jan-2026)

### Description Section
- Use bullet points with `-` character
- Provide clear, concise module description
- Include key functionality points
- Explain integration points if relevant

### Development Log
- Use `-` divider before log section
- Format: `DD-MMM-YYYY - Version X.Y.Z`
- List changes as bullet points with indentation
- Most recent changes at the top
- Include version increments (1.0.0 = stable, 0.x.x = beta/development)

## Rules

### ALWAYS:
- Include file header in every JavaScript module file
- Keep AUTHOR as "Adam Noble - Noble Architecture"
- Use DD-MMM-YYYY date format (e.g., 31-Jan-2026)
- Update development log when making significant changes
- Use bullet points for descriptions and changes
- Match the exact spacing and alignment shown in format

### NEVER:
- Omit the file header from JavaScript files
- Use different date formats
- Leave placeholders like [MODULE NAME] unfilled
- Skip the development log section
- Use inconsistent divider characters
